  <text xml:base="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.philiskos.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc"><body n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.philiskos.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc"><div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.philiskos.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0402_philiskos"><head>ΦΙΛΙΣΚΟΣ</head><div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-philiskos-1">
              <quote>
                <lg>
                  <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-philiskos-1-l1">Ἀρτέον</l>
                  <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0402-philiskos-1-l2">τράπεζαν, ἀπονίψασθαι δοτέον, προσοιστέος</l>
                  <l n="3" xml:id="meineke-0402-philiskos-1-l3">στέφανος, μύρον, σπονδή, λιβανωτός, ἐσχαρίς,</l>
                  <l n="4" xml:id="meineke-0402-philiskos-1-l4">τράγημα δοτέον ἔτι, πλακοῦντος ἁπτέον.</l>
                </lg>
              </quote>
              <note type="source">Athenaeus XIV p. 642 f. de secundarum mensarum deliciis agens: <quote>῎Αλεξις Φιλίσκῳ Ἀρτέον κτλ.</quote>
              </note>
              <note type="apparatus">Vs. 2 Porsonus</note>
              <pb n="499" facs="urn:hathi:hvd.32044079388682:scan:505" />
              <note type="apparatus">
                <quote>ἀπονίψαι</quote>, quod recepit Dindorfius. Sed medium, ni fallor, necessarium est. Suspicabar <quote>τράπεζαν ἀρτέον, | χεῖρας</quote> (vel <quote>ὕδωρ) ἀπονίψασθαι δοτέον</quote>. — Vs. 3 libri ἔσχαρις. — Vs. 4 <quote>τράγημα</quote> Porsonus pro <quote>τραγήματα</quote>.</note>
            </div>
          </div></body></text></TEI>